mn26:25.5 starts: I replied to the Ājīvaka Upaka in stanzas:
# superseded: mn26:25.8 starts: renouncing all, By craving’s ceasing freed.
# superseded: mn26:25.12 starts: in all the world With all its gods,
# superseded: mn26:25.13 starts: because I have No person for my counterpart.
mn26:31.5 starts: Odours cognizable by the nose…
mn26:31.6 starts: Flavours cognizable by the tongue…
mn26:31.7 starts: Tangibles cognizable by the body that are wished for,
mn26:32.6 starts: and when the hunter comes he cannot go
